    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "de3035e6-553f-38a7-8627-02b42d324ed8",
                "word": "pix",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0b840d85-175f-4ba9-9cbd-656dd98f94cb",
                        "entry_id": "de3035e6-553f-38a7-8627-02b42d324ed8",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "pic"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "028bb792-0c66-390c-9203-77272cdcf7c0",
                        "entry_id": "de3035e6-553f-38a7-8627-02b42d324ed8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "plural of pic (“picture”)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of",
                            "informal",
                            "plural",
                            "plural-normally"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6aa946af-353b-4f8b-8dab-e8f958d7e28d",
                                "sense_id": "028bb792-0c66-390c-9203-77272cdcf7c0",
                                "text": "Annual photo contest has brought in some pix by amateurs which are definitely in the professional category."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4edff223-8929-4283-851f-6a7063262902",
                                "sense_id": "028bb792-0c66-390c-9203-77272cdcf7c0",
                                "text": "Photo selection can be tricky with space limitations, Arthur, and we blew that one. Hope the Scott pix in our January issue made you feel better about this."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4537facf-5305-4ea7-98c5-b2581f2876a7",
                                "sense_id": "028bb792-0c66-390c-9203-77272cdcf7c0",
                                "text": "\"But it's not much good piling up the pix if I can't sell them.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "befb7359-6297-4579-97ac-2e034ff5827c",
                                "sense_id": "028bb792-0c66-390c-9203-77272cdcf7c0",
                                "text": "He nervously wrote down Amy’s instructions for what to say and how to behave if the police came back with a search warrant:\n[…]\ntake pix of damage afterward"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f4cb4027-0619-337d-b3b6-e60f072b0ac3",
                        "entry_id": "de3035e6-553f-38a7-8627-02b42d324ed8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Motion pictures; movies."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-normally",
                            "specifically"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "12621f4e-95f7-496c-b86c-456415818579",
                                "sense_id": "f4cb4027-0619-337d-b3b6-e60f072b0ac3",
                                "text": "Mutual has started a campaign to substitute a word for the term “Movies.” It contemplates the use of the word “Pix” and thinks this would be welcomed as a short word for the headline writer and amply descriptive."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "60a8ac46-2bc4-3bb2-95bc-6ec778741610",
                "word": "pix",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ba6b1c2b-2939-4b55-a3d9-14a31c13b793",
                        "entry_id": "60a8ac46-2bc4-3bb2-95bc-6ec778741610",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pixes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "307e8bd0-f35f-3201-9308-5c56c698cf6c",
                        "entry_id": "60a8ac46-2bc4-3bb2-95bc-6ec778741610",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsolete spelling of pyx."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5a9701e-eca1-4261-ac0a-6b1d3acbeee6",
                                "sense_id": "307e8bd0-f35f-3201-9308-5c56c698cf6c",
                                "text": "[F]oraſmuche as we have often and many tymes, to our inwarde regrete and diſpleaſure, ſeen at oure Jen, in diverſe and many Churches of our Realme, the holie Sacrament of the Aulter kept in ful simple and inhoneſt Pixes, ſpecially Pixes of copre and tymbre: we have appointed and commaunded the Treſourer of our Chambre, and Maiſtre of our Juellhouſe, to cauſe to be made furthwith Pixes of ſilver and gilte, in a greate nombre, for the keping of the holie Sacrament of th'Aultre, after the faction of a Pixe that we have cauſed to be delivered to theim, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cb11ceb-f2e5-4713-967b-9b533a4883db",
                                "sense_id": "307e8bd0-f35f-3201-9308-5c56c698cf6c",
                                "text": "[T]he said Tresurer and other Officers of the sayd Mynts, to bring with them, at that tyme and place, all ther Pixes, and ther severall Indentures of Coynag, by and for the holle tyme the said Assaye shall be taken."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69c35a63-9290-41d3-9b1d-c6ecc9c051d6",
                                "sense_id": "307e8bd0-f35f-3201-9308-5c56c698cf6c",
                                "text": "With Croſſes, Relicks, Crucifixes, / Beads, Pictures, Roſaries and Pixes: / The Tools of working out Salvation, / By meer Mechanick Operation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5dae4d4-87cc-417d-b93e-1735fda5f5cf",
                                "sense_id": "307e8bd0-f35f-3201-9308-5c56c698cf6c",
                                "text": "They have Pixes and Chalices for the Bleſſed Sacrament five hundred and fifty, ſome of pure Gold, others of Silver and Criſtal; and among them, is one that was offer'd to our Bleſſed Saviour, by one of the three Kings, when they came to Worſhip him, and brought Preſents."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ffce19f-cfd0-47d3-abf8-10da556584d3",
                                "sense_id": "307e8bd0-f35f-3201-9308-5c56c698cf6c",
                                "text": "The slight breach was fortunately committed by a distant relation of the Archbishop of Toledo, and consisted merely in his entering the church intoxicated, (a rare vice in Spaniards), attempting to drag the matin preacher from the pulpit, and failing in that, getting astride as well as he could on the altar, dashing down the tapers, overturning the vases and the pix, and trying to scratch out, as with the talons of a demon, the painting that hung over the table, uttering all the while the most horrible blasphemies, and even soliciting the portrait of the Virgin in language not to be repeated."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2d11947-3132-490d-ad37-0c072ff33520",
                                "sense_id": "307e8bd0-f35f-3201-9308-5c56c698cf6c",
                                "text": "He [Augustus Pugin] has a most sincere love for his profession, a hearty honest enthusiasm for pixes and piscinas; and though he will never design so much as a pix or piscina thoroughly well, yet better than most of the experimental architects of the day."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "4564a544-e429-37c7-b81a-160df8ad855a",
                "word": "pix",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ee653f1d-adf8-4d9f-8aa3-2e41f4ef051d",
                        "entry_id": "4564a544-e429-37c7-b81a-160df8ad855a",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "pixes"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "256d0409-d3fb-48b9-a354-ecd1391303b2",
                        "entry_id": "4564a544-e429-37c7-b81a-160df8ad855a",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "pixing"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1c1dc106-2b11-4f04-919b-42547b0cc1cf",
                        "entry_id": "4564a544-e429-37c7-b81a-160df8ad855a",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "pixed"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "89d5a8be-1192-4a41-a928-dcd25f466abf",
                        "entry_id": "4564a544-e429-37c7-b81a-160df8ad855a",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "pixed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d28d1537-0849-3dde-aa66-0a578055c9a9",
                        "entry_id": "4564a544-e429-37c7-b81a-160df8ad855a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsolete spelling of pyx."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "61655139-a752-4845-8b91-69c4521f1e44",
                                "sense_id": "d28d1537-0849-3dde-aa66-0a578055c9a9",
                                "text": "The bread that was left of this consecration or breaking, which was so holy as the other, was neither housed nor churched, boxed nor pixed, but remained there still to the householders, to be eaten of whomsoever lusted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5bc4efe-2075-4d28-a9ec-5dde2652d937",
                                "sense_id": "d28d1537-0849-3dde-aa66-0a578055c9a9",
                                "text": "Christ ordained the supper to be a taking matter, an eating matter, a distributing and remembering matter: contrary our mass-men make it a matter, not of taking, but of gazing, peeping, pixing, boxing, carrying, re-carrying, worshipping, stooping, kneeling, knocking, with \"stoop down before,\" \"hold up higher,\" \"I thank God I see my Maker to-day,\" etc. Christ ordained it a table-matter: we turn it to an altar-matter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "018aa56f-78d6-48d7-8a83-a228f24a0278",
                                "sense_id": "d28d1537-0849-3dde-aa66-0a578055c9a9",
                                "text": "[W]hen the money is coined it is not allowed to go out of the mint until pixed; that is, until it had been ascertained, by the assay of one piece taken out of each journeyweight of coin, that it is of standard purity: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2a652f9-5abd-4b2a-a5c7-6a713537f2d4",
                                "sense_id": "d28d1537-0849-3dde-aa66-0a578055c9a9",
                                "text": "The ascertaining whether coin is of the proper standard is in England called \"pixing\" it; and there are occasions on which resort is had for this purpose to an ancient mode of inquisition called the \"trial of the pix,\" before a jury of members of the Goldsmiths' Company."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
